WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:37.833


2
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:38.750
<b>The Pandavas </b>

3
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.958
<b>had just moments ago</b>

4
00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:45.750
<b>blown their conch shells,</b>
<b>resounding through the earth and sky. </b>

5
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.041
<b>The armies on both sides were ready. </b>

6
00:00:49.041 --> 00:00:50.750
<b>Amidst them all, </b>

7
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.916
<b>there was one chariot flying</b>
<b>the flag of Hanuman (Kapi Dhwaja), </b>

8
00:00:55.916 --> 00:01:00.666
<b>a flag with the mighty monkey</b>
<b>god Hanuman on it. </b>

9
00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:04.333
<b>This was the chariot of the great warrior Arjuna. </b>

10
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:10.375
<b>Arjuna surveyed the army of Dhritarashtra's sons</b>
<b>arrayed before him</b>

11
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:14.458
<b>and then raised his weapon.</b>

12
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:19.291


13
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:23.916
<b>Arjuna lifted his Gandiva bow his arrows, </b>

14
00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:28.041
<b>appearing ready to unleash, </b>

15
00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:29.833
<b>but he would not do so. </b>

16
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:35.791
<b>This moment would add a new chapter</b>
<b>in the Mahabharata. </b>

17
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:41.083
<b>The dilemma that would soon</b>
<b>enter Arjuna's mind after this moment </b>

18
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:44.416
<b>would become the very basis of the</b>
<b>Gita's teachings.</b>

19
00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:48.250
<b>Here, Arjuna's flag bears the image of</b>

20
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.666
<b>symbolizing his</b>

21
00:01:49.666 --> 00:01:54.333
<b>support for the Pandavas in the Mahabharata. </b>

22
00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:58.458
<b>Lord Hanuman himself had assured Bhima </b>

23
00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:03.875
<b>that he would always be with them in this battle.</b>

24
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.750


25
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.083
<b>Here, </b>

26
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:15.000
<b>both of us are supporting Arjuna  </b>

27
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.041
<b>and who are we? </b>

28
00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:20.666
<b>We two, </b>

29
00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:21.958
<b>myself</b>

30
00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:26.000
<b>and my dear devotee Hanuman. </b>

31
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.541
<b>How is Hanuman my devotee? </b>

32
00:02:28.541 --> 00:02:30.625
<b>Well, </b>

33
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:37.000
<b>this question must be arising</b>

34
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.708
<b>I am the same as Ramachandra, </b>

35
00:02:40.708 --> 00:02:43.708
<b>one of my own avatars. </b>

36
00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:46.666
<b>Just in a different time. </b>

37
00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.833
<b>In the past,</b>

38
00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.583
<b>as Ramachandra, </b>

39
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:55.041
<b>I vanquished Ravana along</b>
<b>with my devotee Hanuman.</b>

40
00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.708
<b>Even today, if I wish, </b>

41
00:02:57.708 --> 00:03:00.791
<b>or if Hanuman alone desires it, </b>

42
00:03:00.791 --> 00:03:06.083
<b>the outcome of this war ould be decided in the</b>
<b>Pandavas' favor in the very next moment. </b>

43
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:08.166
<b>But</b>

44
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:10.666
<b>this is the Pandavas' time </b>

45
00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:14.125
<b>to showcase their valor, </b>

46
00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:20.125
<b>for Arjuna to demonstrate his prowess.</b>

47
00:03:20.125 --> 00:03:21.333
<b>Often,</b>

48
00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:25.375
<b>it's not necessary to do something for someone. </b>

49
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:29.541
<b>What's necessary</b>
<b>is to instill self-confidence in them, </b>

50
00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:33.916
<b>so that they can accomplish</b>
<b>the task themselves. </b>

51
00:03:33.916 --> 00:03:36.375
<b>When this happens,</b>

52
00:03:36.375 --> 00:03:39.541
<b>the light of that self-confidence spreads further, </b>

53
00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:42.416
<b>inspiring many others. </b>

54
00:03:42.416 --> 00:03:45.750
<b>It awakens self-confidence in them too.</b>

55
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.166
<b>Yes, </b>

56
00:03:47.166 --> 00:03:53.458
<b>there will always be help,</b>
<b>for all those striving for righteousness </b>

57
00:03:53.458 --> 00:03:55.125
<b>from me </b>

58
00:03:55.125 --> 00:03:58.625
<b>and from my Hanuman. </b>

59
00:03:58.625 --> 00:04:01.583
<b>Keep me close to yourself, </b>

60
00:04:01.583 --> 00:04:06.083
<b>keep close to those devotees of mine</b>
<b>who understand the essence of the Gita, </b>

61
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:10.708
<b>and always keep my teachings near you. </b>

62
00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:15.083
<b>There will be only goodness and auspiciousness</b>
<b>in your life.</b>

63
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:19.833


64
00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:22.666
<b>In this great war of the Mahabharata, </b>

65
00:04:22.666 --> 00:04:27.291
<b>I am playing only a supportive role. </b>

66
00:04:27.291 --> 00:04:31.000
<b>I am not wielding any weapons.    </b>

67
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.041
<b>I will only provide guidance.</b>

68
00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.666
<b>I could take up arms </b>

69
00:04:36.666 --> 00:04:41.125
<b>and make the Pandavas victorious</b>
<b>in the very next moment, </b>

70
00:04:41.125 --> 00:04:42.625
<b>but then </b>

71
00:04:42.625 --> 00:04:46.750
<b>all the credit would go to me, right? </b>

72
00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.500
<b>How would you remember, </b>

73
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:55.208
<b>how would the earth remember the</b>
<b>valor of these five brothers?</b>

74
00:04:55.208 --> 00:05:01.541
<b>A victory that someone else serves on</b>
<b>a platter is far less significant </b>

75
00:05:01.541 --> 00:05:04.916
<b>than a victory you have strived for.  </b>

76
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:06.208
<b>Because in the latter case, </b>

77
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:10.750
<b>learning grows along with the victory, </b>

78
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.416
<b>your own strength also increases.</b>

79
00:05:15.416 --> 00:05:19.291
<b>It is easy to remove stones</b>

80
00:05:19.291 --> 00:05:21.625
<b>but it is better </b>

81
00:05:21.625 --> 00:05:23.375
<b>to teach them, </b>

82
00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:24.916
<b>to show them </b>

83
00:05:24.916 --> 00:05:28.291
<b>how to remove the stones themselves, </b>

84
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:29.791
<b>to break them, </b>

85
00:05:29.791 --> 00:05:32.541
<b>and to move forward.</b>

86
00:05:32.541 --> 00:05:34.875
<b>Now you tell me,</b>

87
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:36.291
<b>are you</b>

88
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:38.875
<b>somehow making your younger ones </b>

89
00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:40.791
<b>or your children </b>

90
00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:48.250
<b>dependent on you by removing every</b>
<b>difficulty from their path? </b>

91
00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.250
<b>Guide them, </b>

92
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.125
<b>give them just a little support, </b>

93
00:05:54.125 --> 00:05:56.125
<b>and then see </b>

94
00:05:56.125 --> 00:06:02.583
<b>what immense capacity they have</b>
<b>within themselves to fight the duels of their lives.</b>

95
00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:04.625
<b>Make them independent, </b>

96
00:06:04.625 --> 00:06:06.958
<b>not subservient.</b>

97
00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.666


98
00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:15.541
<b>The conch shells have been blown</b>
<b>on both sides for war, </b>

99
00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.166
<b>the armies are eager </b>

100
00:06:17.166 --> 00:06:20.583
<b>to send each other to the jaws of death, </b>

101
00:06:20.583 --> 00:06:25.375
<b>and Arjuna too has raised his Gandiva bow. </b>

102
00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:27.416
<b>But </b>

103
00:06:27.416 --> 00:06:30.958
<b>he will pause here, </b>

104
00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>and not only that, </b>

105
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.333
<b>because of him,</b>

106
00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:38.500
<b>the war of the Mahabharata will halt </b>

107
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.958
<b>for some time.</b>

108
00:06:40.958 --> 00:06:43.916
<b>There is no lack of strength in Arjuna, </b>

109
00:06:43.916 --> 00:06:47.708
<b>his valor is also immense, </b>

110
00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:49.291
<b>yet he </b>

111
00:06:49.291 --> 00:06:54.416
<b>will stop before taking the next step, </b>

112
00:06:54.416 --> 00:06:58.125
<b>because that is the right thing to do.</b>

113
00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:03.791
<b>Even if you certainly have the ability</b>
<b>to do any great work,</b>

114
00:07:03.791 --> 00:07:05.041
<b>But </b>

115
00:07:05.041 --> 00:07:11.666
<b>to ponder before walking on a path from</b>
<b>which you cannot return.</b>

116
00:07:11.666 --> 00:07:16.083
<b>it is extremely important to think a little, </b>

117
00:07:16.083 --> 00:07:27.958
<b>to examine your goals, to consult with experienced</b>
<b>people before proceeding furth</b>

118
00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:31.916
<b>Especially when the goal is big.</b>

119
00:07:31.916 --> 00:07:35.041
<b>The bigger the goal, </b>

120
00:07:35.041 --> 00:07:37.833
<b>the greater the caution.</b>

